## Project overview

For my data science senior project at BYU–Idaho, I am exploring
whether machine learning can distinguish mental stress from
physical activity using wearable-device data.

I chose this project because I am interested in the health and
wellness industry. I want to combine that interest with my
experience in Python, data cleaning, and machine learning to
build something useful for my portfolio.

The project has two main goals:

1. Train and evaluate a model using research data collected
   during stress and exercise sessions.
2. Build a Python package that makes loading, cleaning, and
   preparing wearable data easier.

I will begin with the research dataset's format. Supporting
exports from Fitbit, Apple Watch, or Garmin is a later goal
that will depend on which signals are available. Performance
on other devices will need separate testing.

